WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.354
Week four.

00:00:01.404 --> 00:00:06.600
Managing brands with creativity and humanity, with former Telstra CMO Brent Smart.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.092
Marketing is a battle for memory.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.413
So job one is making the brand memorable,

00:00:11.463 --> 00:00:13.784
and the biggest risk is taking no risk.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.058
And creativity pays.

00:00:16.108 --> 00:00:17.408
Against the average ad,

00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:18.747
creative work returns two and a half times the revenue growth,

00:00:18.797 --> 00:00:22.088
and four times the profit.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.324
When Telstra asked people to draw how the brand felt,

00:00:24.374 --> 00:00:26.913
they drew a bully in a suit.

00:00:26.963 --> 00:00:28.654
You can argue with a chart.

00:00:28.704 --> 00:00:30.868
You can't argue with that drawing.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:34.520
Only about fifteen percent of buyers are in market right now.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:38.579
The other eighty five percent need brand building, so they remember you later.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:42.521
The benchmark is sixty percent brand, forty activation.

00:00:42.571 --> 00:00:44.061
Telstra was at twenty.

00:00:44.111 --> 00:00:46.148
His first move was fifty fifty.

00:00:46.198 --> 00:00:49.279
Marketing ROI rose from six to over ten.

00:00:49.867 --> 00:00:51.804
The whistling ad was hated at launch,

00:00:51.854 --> 00:00:54.259
then got thirty million organic TikTok views.

00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:56.547
If it's not bold, it's dumb.
